@startuml
!theme plain
|a_default| Default
|a_default|
start
:Start process;
:Items returned by customer or picked up by delivery crew;
:v1: Return method ({Customer returns items to store, Delivery crew picks up items at event site}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v1 = 'Customer returns items to store'])
:Continue via customer return;
else ([v1 = 'Delivery crew picks up items at event site'])
:Continue via delivery pickup;
endif
:Count and compare items to contract;
:Order status after count;
:v2: Order status ({All items returned, Items missing, Items damaged}); <<objectSignal>>
switch ()
case ([v2 = 'Items damaged'])
:Email customer damage and additional charges;
:Email customer missing items and replacement charges;
:v4: Customer return missing ({Customer returns missing items, Customer does not return missing items}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v4 = 'Customer returns missing items'])
:Customer returns missing items;
else ([v4 = 'Customer does not return missing items'])
:Customer does not return missing items;
endif
:Finally, when the process is complete, it ends;
:v5: Repair status ({Can be repaired, Cannot be repaired}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v5 = 'Can be repaired'])
:Repair items and add to inventory;
else ([v5 = 'Cannot be repaired'])
:Discard items and email customer replacement charges;
endif
:Items disposition after repair;
:v6: Final disposition ({Packed for existing order, Stored for future orders}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v6 = 'Packed for existing order'])
:Items are packed for an existing order;
else ([v6 = 'Stored for future orders'])
:Items are stored for future orders;
endif
:Once again, when the process is complete, it ends;
:Email customer with replacement charges;
stop
case ([v2 = 'All items returned'])
:Items are packed for an existing order;
case ([v2 = 'Items missing'])
:Items are stored for future orders;
:Temporarily remove damaged items from inventory;
endswitch
@enduml